NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-supabase-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-keyWe have a Vercel production build failure in commit 836c3f8.

Fix ONLY the current build/type error first. Do not redesign anything and do not change unrelated code.

Vercel error:

app/(dashboard)/admin/providers/providers-client-view.tsx(98,213):
error TS2322: Type 'string' is not assignable to type '"gemini" | "openai_compatible"'.

The relevant code currently has:

const [form, setForm] = useState({
  slug: provider?.slug || '',
  displayName: provider?.display_name || '',
  adapter: provider?.adapter || 'gemini',
  primaryModel: provider?.primary_model || '',
  fallbackModels: provider?.fallback_models?.join(', ') || '',
  baseUrl: provider?.base_url || '',
  apiKey: '',
  isActive: provider?.is_active ?? true,
  isDefault: provider?.is_default ?? false,
});

And later:

adapter: form.adapter as 'gemini' | 'openai_compatible',

There is a TypeScript inference problem because the initial useState object causes `form.adapter` to be inferred as a generic string.

Fix this properly by defining an explicit form type, for example:

type ProviderFormState = {
  slug: string;
  displayName: string;
  adapter: 'gemini' | 'openai_compatible';
  primaryModel: string;
  fallbackModels: string;
  baseUrl: string;
  apiKey: string;
  isActive: boolean;
  isDefault: boolean;
};

Then make useState use that type:

const [form, setForm] = useState<ProviderFormState>({
  ...
  adapter: provider?.adapter ?? 'gemini',
  ...
});

Make sure the select/onChange also safely converts the value to the allowed union:

onChange={(e) =>
  setForm({
    ...form,
    adapter: e.target.value as ProviderFormState['adapter'],
  })
}

Do NOT simply suppress the error with @ts-ignore, @ts-expect-error, or by disabling TypeScript checking.

After fixing it, run ALL of these from the repository root:

pnpm type-check
pnpm lint
pnpm build

If any of them fail, fix the actual issue and rerun them.

Then check git status.

If all three pass, commit the fix with:

fix(admin): fix provider form adapter typing

Then push to origin/main.

IMPORTANT:
- Do not change the provider architecture.
- Do not remove the admin provider functionality.
- Do not change Gemini models.
- Do not modify environment variables.
- Do not make unrelated UI changes.
- The goal is simply to get the current admin provider implementation compiling cleanly in Vercel production.